From c7363aa963712846984826d7bd5a2982ee8bb2e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Trotter <james@jamesat.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:20:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] accounts: account-bound operator status and vhosts from
 auth-script

An auth-script response may now include operClass, whoisLine and vhost.
On a successful login the client is opered up into that oper class at
registration (or at once for a login after registration) and the vhost is
stored as the account's HostServ vhost. The same grants can be applied at
any time, including to connected clients, via POST /v1/account_grants. On
rehash, account-bound opers follow their class's new definition and are
de-opered if it was removed. /OPER opers are never affected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
