 The response format is the same as `/v1/ns/saget`.
 
+`/v1/account_grants`
+--------------------
+
+This endpoint grants or revokes account-bound operator status and sets an account's vhost, with the same semantics as the optional `operClass`, `whoisLine` and `vhost` keys of an `auth-script` response (see the manual), and applies them immediately to the account's connected clients. The request is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `accountName`: string, name of the account
+* `operClass`: string, optional: the name of an `oper-classes` entry, or the empty string to revoke account-bound operator status. Omit it to leave operator status alone. Clients that used `/OPER` are not affected.
+* `whoisLine`: string, optional, overrides the class's `whois-line`
+* `vhost`: string, optional: the account's new vhost, or the empty string to remove it. Omit it to leave the vhost alone.
+
+The response is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `success`: boolean, whether the request succeeded
+* `clients`: number, how many connected clients of the account had their operator status synced (0 if `operClass` was omitted)
+* `errorCode`: string, optional, machine-readable description of the error. Possible values: `ACCOUNT_DOES_NOT_EXIST`, `UNKNOWN_OPER_CLASS`, `INVALID_VHOST`, `FEATURE_DISABLED`, `UNKNOWN_ERROR`.
+* `error`: string, optional, human-readable description of the failure
+
 `/v1/ns/saregister`
 -------------------
 
